  "answer": "This has been reported before. The Command Palette Dock doesn't remember the network adapter picked with 'Next Network'. After a restart it goes back to a different adapter, usually the unused Ethernet one, and shows zeros. PowerToys#48858 describes the same behaviour on 0.100.1, and several other users confirmed it there. I found no fix in the archive. There is a workaround from PowerToys#47430. After each reboot, open the network flyout (click the network stats) and select the adapter you actually use, which is your Wi-Fi. If the values are blank, disable and re-enable the Dock in the Command Palette settings. Another option is to disable the unused Ethernet adapter, which one commenter did. Add your report and your bug report ZIP to #48858 so the team can track it."
 },
